# atlas-rsync sudoers grant (filename retained for install-path continuity:
# /etc/sudoers.d/atlas-rsync). Superseded the raw-rsync grant on 2026-05-24.
#
# Lets the unprivileged atlas user refresh the root-owned, chattr+i-sealed
# production lib tree /usr/local/lib/atlas from the atlas-core source tree, via a
# SINGLE pinned wrapper with NO arguments. Any deviation from the exact command
# requires a password. Atlas has no other sudo; this is the narrowest grant that
# lets the scheduled git-sync mirror the lib while keeping the anti-tamper seal
# intact.
#
# 2026-05-24 (session 3969d6a0 follow-up — git-sync 3-copy reconciliation).
# The prior grant was a raw `rsync -aL --delete /home/atlas/.atlas/lib/
# /usr/local/lib/atlas/`. Two problems forced this change:
#   (1) gap-2 sealed the prod tree with `chattr -R +i`, so a raw `rsync --delete`
#       into it now FAILS (immutable files). The mirror needs unseal -> rsync ->
#       reseal, which rsync alone cannot do.
#   (2) granting atlas a raw `chattr -i` verb would let a compromised atlas
#       account unseal the prod tree at will, defeating the seal.
# Fix: grant atlas NOPASSWD on a single root-owned wrapper that performs the
# whole unseal -> rsync (from a root-only staging tree, only AFTER an import-probe
# passes) -> reseal -> verify cycle, fail-closed. Atlas can trigger the exact
# sanctioned cycle but cannot run arbitrary chattr/rsync, and never sees the
# unsealed tree as writable (prod stays root:root throughout the brief window).
#
# WRAPPER INTEGRITY IS LOAD-BEARING: the wrapper MUST be installed root:root 0755
# in the root-only dir /usr/local/libexec/atlas AND sealed `chattr +i`. If atlas
# can modify the wrapper, this grant degrades to arbitrary-root-exec. Wrapper
# source of truth: atlas-engineering scripts/mirror-lib.sh. Invoked by the
# scheduled atlas-engineering scripts/git-sync.sh (deployed to
# /home/atlas/git-sync.sh). Full runbook + threat notes:
# ~/.atlas/plans/host-executor-lib-security-finding-2026-05-23.md §10.
#
# Why root-owned destination: the seal works only if the dir + contents are
# root-owned; the wrapper's rsync runs as root, preserving that invariant.
#
# Install on the VPS (supervised root step, requires real root / docker-root):
#
#   install -d -m 755 -o root -g root /usr/local/libexec/atlas
#   install -m 0755 -o root -g root \
#       /home/atlas/.atlas/scripts/mirror-lib.sh \
#       /usr/local/libexec/atlas/mirror-lib.sh
#   chattr +i /usr/local/libexec/atlas/mirror-lib.sh
#   install -m 440 -o root -g root \
#       /home/atlas/nanoclaw/infra/sudoers.d/atlas-rsync \
#       /etc/sudoers.d/atlas-rsync
#   visudo -c                                   # validate, must report OK
#   sudo -u atlas sudo -n /usr/local/libexec/atlas/mirror-lib.sh; echo "rc=$?"  # smoke
#
# Removal (rollback):
#
#   rm /etc/sudoers.d/atlas-rsync
#   chattr -i /usr/local/libexec/atlas/mirror-lib.sh
#   rm /usr/local/libexec/atlas/mirror-lib.sh
#   visudo -c
#
atlas ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/libexec/atlas/mirror-lib.sh
